## Key Takeaways
1.PowerShell works with objects instead of only plain text, and objects contain useful properties and methods.
2. Get-Member can be used to inspect an object and identify its properties, methods, and object type.
3. Where-Object can filter objects based on property values so an administrator can focus on specific information.
